{
  "about": [
    "Shared cases for what ticking a step does to its big task. Each holds the tasks just AFTER the tick (the ticked step is already done), the ticked step's id, the big tasks the SERVER finishes (server/src/steps.ts planFinish), and the end state after the app has run its own repair.",
    "Read by two tests: server/src/steps.test.ts runs planFinish over them and checks serverFinishes exactly; client/src/lib/settle-parity.test.ts runs the app's settleCompletions and healStuckParents and checks (a) the server never finishes what the app would not, (b) the server's finishes followed by the app's repair reach endState, and (c) the app on its own reaches endState too. (b) with (c) is the proof that leaving a case to the app loses nothing.",
    "Times are epoch ms (small numbers on purpose, the dates do not matter, only the order). Each task field is the client's name: id, title, done, createdAt, completedAt, deletedAt, parentId, parentTitle, silentParent, openParent, recurrence, completedDates, combinedFrom. endState lists done, silentParent, openParent (true, false or null for unknown) and deleted, plus completedAt for a big task that finishes.",
    "Not here on purpose: a round of NONE at the direct parent (reachable only with clock skew). The app's own tick would finish it, the server leaves it, and the repair brings it back, the safe direction (design doc, section 1c)."
  ],
  "day": "2026-10-18",
  "now": 10000000,
